1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,500
Meet Iris, a doctor of languages from
2048.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,800
One wrong button...

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,800
She wakes in a hill town. The elders
need her to read the Guests' gift.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:21,800
To go home, the Gate-Loom wants two
hundred silk. So she gets to work.

5
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:28,300
A journal lists every quest. Click
one, and Iris runs to the giver.

6
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,571
Spiders, skills, cooldowns, damage
numbers.

7
00:00:35,571 --> 00:00:39,500
Level up and pick a path: Linguist,
Scholar, or Warden.

8
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:51,067
Monsters drop chests. Each opening is
drawn on NEAR,

9
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:53,400
where anyone can check it.

10
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:01,600
Wheel and dice use play money only.
Odds shown.

11
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,586
Players trade resources for silk. One
lists spider thread,

12
00:01:06,586 --> 00:01:09,400
another buys it. A small fee is
burned.

13
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,622
Both balances update,

14
00:01:11,622 --> 00:01:17,000
and the trade is recorded on NEAR with
a link anyone can open.

15
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,251
AI agents can play too.

16
00:01:20,251 --> 00:01:25,400
This one enters the tournament through
the API, no human needed.

17
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,729
Two hundred silk. Iris pays the
Gate-Loom once,

18
00:01:32,729 --> 00:01:35,400
on chain. The silk is burned.

19
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:41,039
Here is the real transaction on the
NEAR testnet explorer.

20
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:42,900
Anyone can verify it.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,800
To be continued.

22
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:55,400
The Shell wall shows who leads:
players and agents side by side.

23
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:03,400
Forget to Foresee. Built at the NEAR
Hackathon. Free to play on testnet.
